{"type":"assistant","uuid":"f05ecae6-1e65-4530-9e24-473b63b4f0ae","session_id":"df21ea8c-4013-4720-afce-f68bcbc7f08c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"f05ecae6-1e65-4530-9e24-473b63b4f0ae","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the issue clearly. Let me trace through the code:\n\n1. In `ServerSettingsFragment.testConnection()`, it calls `Util.setActiveServer(context, serverId)` to set the active server.\n2. Then it calls `MusicServiceFactory.getMusicService(context)` which calls `createSubsonicApiClient(context)`.\n3. `createSubsonicApiClient` reads the instance from `preferences.getInt(Constants.PREFERENCES_KEY_SERVER_INSTANCE, 1)`.\n\nThe key issue is: `Util.setActiveServer` calls `MusicServiceFactory.resetMusicService()` first, which is good. Then it sets the instance. \n\nLooking at the `setActiveServer` method, it resets the music service, gets the preferences, and commits the new instance value. The default for `PREFERENCES_KEY_SERVER_INSTANCE` is 1, and in `createSubsonicApiClient`, it reads this instance value to determine which server configuration to use.\n\nNow examining `getActiveServer`, it also defaults to 1 when retrieving the current instance. When `testConnection()` runs, it retrieves the current active server, sets it to the target `serverId`, then fetches the music service. The logic seems sound at first glance, but I'm noticing something about how the preferences are being read or applied that might be causing the issue.\n\nLooking back at the bug report, the core problem is that the connection attempt goes to localhost even though a valid server URL was entered. This points to either the server URL not being persisted correctly to preferences, or the wrong URL being retrieved when the connection is attempted. In `onPreferenceChange`, when the server URL preference changes, it validates the URL and stores it in shared preferences with the server ID as a key prefix.\n\nWhen `testConnection()` is called, it gets the current active server instance from `Util.getActiveServer()`, which defaults to 1. Then `MusicServiceFactory.getMusicService()` retrieves that same instance value and uses it to construct the server URL by looking up the preferences with the instance number as a suffix. The logic chains together—`serverId` from the fragment arguments should match the instance number used to retrieve and store the URL in preferences. Now I'm checking what the XML resource `server_settings` actually contains. I'm tracing through the logic to understand why localhost is being connected to instead of the actual server URL. The issue seems to be in how the server instance ID is being used when creating the music service during the connection test. I'm wondering if `getPreferences()` is pointing to the wrong SharedPreferences file or if there's a mismatch in how the server ID is being retrieved and stored across the different calls.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
